	BP=|USA|
	BD=|1871|
	DD=|1958|
	NT=|Graduated from Hamilton College in 1891, and then
	worked at the <i>New York Sun</i> until 1900. Worked
	at <i>McClure's Magazine</i> from 1901 through 1905.
	His <I>The Great American Fraud</I>, which expanded on
	his magazine articles exposing fradulent patent
	medicines, help the passage of the Pure Fodd and Drug
	Act of 1906. In 1915, he began a similar persuit of
	advertising practices in the <i>New York Tribune</i>.|
