Brian W. Aldiss {
	LN=|Aldiss, Brian Wilson|
	BP=|UK|
	BD=|1925|
	NT=|Served in the Royal Signal Corp in Burma and Sumatra during WWII.
	Afterward he worked as an assistant in a bookshop, and began writing
	fiction about the book trade, which was later collected in
	<i>The Brightfount Diaries</i>. He became editor of the
	<i>The Oxford Mail</i> in 1958, and was the first President of the
	British Science Fiction Association. Aldiss became closely aligned
	with the British New Wave in the mid 60's, while establishing himself
	as an important SF anthologist and critic.|
}
Thomas Bailey Aldrich {
	LN=|Aldrich, Thomas Bailey|
	BP=|USA|
	BD=|1836|
	DD=|1907|
	NT=|Poet, journalist, editor, and short-story writer. Served as a
	war correspondent for the New York Tribune during the Civil War. Was
	literary critic for the <i>New York Evening Mirror</i>, editor for
	the <i>Home Journal</i>, and eventually editor of <i>The Atlantic
	Monthly</i>. Influencial in the development of the short story form
	in America.|
