Edmond Hamilton {
	LN=|Hamilton, Edmond Moore|
	BP=|USA|
	BD=|1904|
	DD=|1977|
	NT=|Hamilton majored in physics in Pennsylvania, but never graduated. He
	instead made his first appearance in <i>Weird Tales</i> in 1926. His 1928
	"Crashing Suns" (in, yes - <i>Weird Tales</i>) helped to define the newly-developing
	space opera genre. He quickly made a name for himself with his "Interstellar Patrol"
	series of science fiction stories, which all appeared in <i>Weird Tales</i> 1929-1930,
	and which %%A,A. Merritt%% tried to publish in book form in the early 30's.
	In the late 1930's, Standard Magazines created the magazine
	<i>Captain Future</i>, for which Hamilton wrote a novel for each issue.
	These were continued in <i>Startling Stories</i> in 1945-1946 and later
	1950-1951. He was married to noted SF author %%A,Leigh Brackett%%.|
}
