Chesley Bonestell {
	LN=|Bonestell, Chesley|
	BP=|USA|
	BD=|1888|
	DD=|1986|
	NT=|Artist who studied at the Columbia University School of
	Architecture and worked primarily as an architectural draftsman
	from 1910 to 1938.  Worked on the <i>Illustrated London News</i>
	from the end of World War I to 1927, when he returned to New York.
	In the USA he participated in the designs for structures like
	the Chrysler Building and the Golden Gate Bridge. He began
	producing astronomical artwork for <i>Life</i> in the 1940s,
	published his first SF cover in 1947 (<i>Astounding</i>), and
	thereafter appeared on numerous covers of <i>Fantasy & Science Fiction</i>
	throughout the 1950s.  The Chesley Bonestell Interactive
	%%H,Art Gallery##http://www.secapl.com/bonestell/top.html%%,
	is maintained by Kathryn Humm.|
