Terry Dowling {
	LN=|Dowling, Terry|
	BP=|Sydney, Australia|
	BD=|1947|
	NT=|Terry Dowling is one of Australia's most acclaimed writers of science fiction,
	fantasy and horror. He is author of <i>Rynosseros</i>, <i>Blue Tyson</i> and
	<i>Twilight Beach</i> (the Tom Rynosseros saga), <i>Wormwood</i>, <i>The Man Who Lost
	Red</i> and <i>An Intimate Knowledge of the Night</i>, and editor (with Dr Van Ikin) of
	<i>Mortal Fire: Best Australian SF</i> and senior editor of <i>The Essential Ellison</i>. As well as
	being reviewer of science fiction, fantasy and horror for The Australian, he is also
	a musician and songwriter, with eight years of appearances on the ABC's
	Mr Squiggle & Friends, and is a Communications lecturer at a large Sydney college.
	He has been called "one of our finest futurists" (Independent Monthly) and "one of
	the finest imaginative minds of the 1990s" (Canberra Times).|
