William R. Eakin {
	LN=|Eakin, William R.|
	BP=|Georgia, USA|
	BD=|1958|
	PS=|Bill Eakin|
	NT=|Biographic Data: William R. Eakin (Bill) has sold some 40 science
	fiction and fantasy stories over the past two years to places like Non-Stop SF,
	Realms of Fantasy, The Magazine of Fantasy & Science Fiction and Space
	and Time. His numerous "Redgunk" stories - speculative satires set in
	mythical town of Redgunk, Mississippi - have received special attention.
	One Redgunk story won the 1995 Andre Norton SF/Fantasy Award; another
	received the First Place prize in the 1996 North Texas Professional
	Writer's Association's Fiction Contest; yet another received 1st place
	in the 1996 Best of Soft SF Contest. In addition to writing
	fiction, Bill has served as editor for a series of books on ecology and
	world religions (Orbis press). Besides writing, he teaches part-time at
	a college and works as something of a househusband for his wife,
	9-year-old son and 6-year-old twins on a large property they call the
	"Thicket" (after the safeplace in "Bambi").|
}
