Erle Stanley Gardner {
	LN=|Gardner, Erle Stanley|
	BP=|Malden, Massachusetts, USA|
	BD=|1889|
	DD=|1970|
	PS=|Charles Green;Kyle Corning;Grant Holiday|
	NT=|Creator of Perry Mason. Settled with his family in Oroville, California in 1902.
	Worked as a legal clerk and passing the California bar in 1911. Earned a reputation
	for defending the Chinese community with unconventional defenses. Formed the law firm
	of Orr and Gardner in 1916 in Ventura CA. Started writing fiction in 1921. His first
	published story was "Nellie's Naughty Nighty" appearing in <i>Breezy Stories</i>. The
	first Perry Mason book (<i>The Case of the Velvet Claws</i>) was published in 1933.
	There are several Erle Stanley Gardner webpages. These are two good starting places:
	%%H,www.grooviespad.com/esg##http://www.grooviespad.com/esg/%%,
	%%H,www.phantoms.com/gardner##http://www.phantoms.com/gardner/%%.|
