Honoré de Balzac {
	LN=|de Balzac, Honoré|
	BD=|1799|
	DD=|1850|
	BP=|Tours, France|
	NT=|Generally considered the creator of realism in literature and
	one of the greatest fiction writers of all time. Schooled in Paris,
	Balzac worked for a lawyer at age 16, writing plays and novels at
	night. After the failure of his fiction, he attempted to start a
	business, which also failed. In 1929 he finally published his
	first novel, and spent the bulk of his life in Paris. As with many
	SF writers, Balzac had a plan to unify his novels into a unified
	series, referring to it as <i>The Human Comedy</i>, which eventually
	encompassed some 90 novels and novellas.|
}
